jobs.description:
**Entity** : Oracle America, Inc.  

**Job Duties** : Design, develop, troubleshoot and/or test/QA software. As a member of the software engineering division, apply knowledge of software architecture to perform tasks associated with developing, debugging, or designing software applications or operating systems according to provided design specifications. Build enhancements within an existing software architecture and/or suggest improvements to the architecture. As a developer in the cloud services area, work in an agile development model and deliver monthly releases for cloud deployment. Collaborate with teams across Oracle Cloud Infrastructure (OCI), Site Reliability Engineering (SRE), Cloud Support, and other partner organizations to deliver integrated cloud services. Define, develop, and deploy new features for the cloud service. May telecommute. (385\.28314\)  

Employer will accept a Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or related technical field and 2 years of experience in the job offered or in a Software Developer\-related occupation.
Position requires:
* Java;
* Computer and network architecture;
* Systems design, including microservices and cloud;
* C and C\+\+;
* Data structures and algorithms;
* UI development;
* Networks and security;
* Database management systems;
* Operating systems

**Entity** : Oracle America, Inc.  

**Job Duties** : Design, develop, troubleshoot and/or test/QA software. As a member of the software engineering division, apply knowledge of software architecture to perform tasks associated with developing, debugging, or designing software applications or operating systems according to provided design specifications. Build enhancements within an existing software architecture and/or suggest improvements to the architecture. May telecommute. (385\.32474\)  

Employer will accept a Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Information Technology, or related technical field and 4 years of experience in the job offered or in a Software Developer\-related occupation.  

Position requires:
* Programming, including system\-level languages Go, C\+\+, or Rust;
* Object\-oriented and functional programming and Distributed Systems;
* Cloud\-native patterns including microservices;
* Networking \& Protocols;
* Systems Design, including designing, decomposing, and documenting medium\-scale systems;
* Testing \& Automation, including writing unit, integration, and regression tests;
* CI/CD pipelines, mocking frameworks, and test\-driven development;
* Debugging \& Ops Readiness, including tools lperf, strace, tcpdump, logs, and metrics; and
* Writing runbooks.

